CORE
main.c
--unwind 2 --rounds 3 --yaml-witness -
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^- segment: \[{waypoint: {type: .function_enter., action: .follow., location: {file_name: .main.c., line: 18}, thread_id: 0}}\]$
^- segment: \[{waypoint: {type: .function_enter., action: .follow., location: {file_name: .main.c., line: 9}, thread_id: 1}}\]$
^- segment: \[{waypoint: {type: .target., action: .follow., location: {file_name: .main.c., line: 5}, thread_id: 2}}\]$
--
^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
thread_id: 3}
--
In a YAML witness the k-th thread creation in the witness names thread k.
Symex numbers the threads of main first, so the grandchild, created by thread
1 before main creates its second thread, is thread 3 in the trace but the
second creation in the witness: the target has to say thread_id 2.
